      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "A middle-aged man presented with intermittent gross haematuria and dull aching left flank pain for 1\u2005month. He was a chronic smoker for 15\u2005years. Contrast-enhanced CT scan of the abdomen detected a 4.5×3.0×2.5\u2005cm, heterogeneous and poorly contrast-enhancing mass in the left renal sinus and upper ureteric region causing narrowing of the pelviureteric junction and upper ureter. Considering it to be a transitional cell carcinoma of upper urinary tract, the patient underwent laparoscopic radical nephroureterectomy. Histopathology revealed the mass to be a neurofibroma in the renal sinus extending around the upper ureter."
      },
